# PART 02 — THE FICTIONAL WORLD

## The universe

The world is built around a fictional digital infrastructure created by an organization whose existence has been erased from public records.

This infrastructure was designed to preserve information, monitor distributed systems, investigate digital anomalies, and operate across independent nodes.

Over time, something happened.

The system was officially shut down.

Its operators disappeared.

Its records were deleted.

Its servers were supposedly destroyed.

But the network never completely went offline.

Fragments continued communicating.

Some nodes continued processing.

Certain archives continued receiving data.

Unknown processes remained active.

And now the system is accessible again.

The user enters through an unidentified access point.

They do not know who built the environment.

They do not know who is sending signals.

They do not know whether the information inside is trustworthy.

They do not know whether the system is broken, deliberately operating, or responding to them.

Everything inside the universe must have a coherent fictional history.

Develop:

- The origin of the network.
- The organization behind it.
- The creation of Project ROOT.
- The existence of Ghostnet.
- The original purpose of Blackbox.
- Major historical incidents.
- Missing operators.
- Abandoned facilities.
- Failed experiments.
- Digital anomalies.
- Internal conflicts.
- Multiple factions.
- Hidden motives.
- A chronological timeline.
- A central mystery.
- Several smaller mysteries that eventually connect to it.

Do not explain the lore through a giant introduction.

Reveal it through exploration.

